---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="About Us"
  description="Learn about Charles Michael Sports Hub, its founder Michael Charles James Karuga, co-founders Moses Kamau and Ngugi Kinyanjui, and its work in sport, youth development and community programmes."
>

  <!-- Page Hero -->
  <section class="bg-navy text-white py-24" style="clip-path: polygon(0 0, 100% 0, 100% 88%, 0 100%);">
    <div class="max-w-7xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8">
      <p class="section-subtitle text-red-brand mb-3">Our Story</p>
      <h1 class="font-display font-black text-4xl sm:text-6xl md:text-7xl text-white leading-none mb-6">About Charles Michael Sports Hub</h1>
      <p class="font-body text-blue-100 text-xl max-w-2xl leading-relaxed">
        A sports hub built on discipline, pride and a clear vision for Kenyan athletes.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Story & Mission -->
  <section class="py-20 bg-white">
    <div class="max-w-7xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 grid lg:grid-cols-2 gap-16 items-start">
      <div class="reveal">
        <p class="section-subtitle">Our Mission</p>
        <h2 class="section-title mb-6">Built for the Long Game</h2>
        <p class="font-body text-gray-600 text-lg leading-relaxed mb-5">
          Charles Michael Sports Hub is a community sports organisation founded in Limuru, Kenya. We create welcoming opportunities for children, young people and adults to train, compete and grow. Taekwondo is our flagship programme, where athletes develop their skills in a disciplined and supportive environment.
        </p>
        <p class="font-body text-gray-600 text-lg leading-relaxed mb-5">
          We believe sport changes lives through more than medals and trophies. Regular training helps people build discipline, respect, confidence and perseverance. We are here to develop athletes and support the people and communities around them.
        </p>
        <p class="font-body text-gray-600 text-lg leading-relaxed">
          Our long-term ambition is to host an internationally recognised taekwondo open in Kenya, working with the Kenya Taekwondo Federation and the appropriate governing bodies. We are building towards that goal through consistent training, competition and community partnerships.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="reveal space-y-6">
        <div class="bg-bluegrey border-l-4 border-navy p-7 rounded-r-lg">
          <h3 class="font-display font-bold text-2xl text-navy mb-2">Why Limuru?</h3>
          <p class="font-body text-gray-600 leading-relaxed">
            Limuru sits at the centre of Kiambu County, with strong school networks and a community of families who value sport. It is the right place to build something lasting.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="bg-bluegrey border-l-4 border-red-brand p-7 rounded-r-lg">
          <h3 class="font-display font-bold text-2xl text-navy mb-2">Context: Kenya on the World Stage</h3>
          <p class="font-body text-gray-600 leading-relaxed">
            Nairobi hosted the first World Taekwondo Under-21 Championships in December 2025, bringing together 452 athletes from 75 nations. The event highlighted the potential of taekwondo in Kenya and the opportunities for local athletes to take part in the sport at the highest levels.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Founder -->
  <section class="py-20 bg-bluegrey">
    <div class="max-w-7xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 grid lg:grid-cols-3 gap-12 items-start">
      <div class="reveal lg:col-span-1">
        <img
          src="/images/michael-charles-founder.webp"
          alt="Michael Charles James Karuga, founder of Charles Michael Sports Hub"
          class="w-full aspect-square object-cover object-top rounded-lg shadow-xl border-4 border-red-brand/30"
          loading="lazy"
          decoding="async"
        />
      </div>
      <div class="reveal lg:col-span-2">
        <p class="section-subtitle">Founder</p>
        <h2 class="section-title mb-2">Michael Charles James Karuga</h2>
        <p class="font-display text-2xl text-red-brand font-semibold mb-6">Black Belt, Taekwondo</p>

        <!-- Credentials block -->
        <div class="grid sm:grid-cols-2 gap-4 mb-8">
          {[
            { label: 'Belt Grade', value: '2nd Dan Black Belt' },
            { label: 'Years Coaching', value: '9 years' },
            { label: 'Certifications', value: 'World Taekwondo and Kenya Taekwondo Federation certificates' },
            { label: 'Competitions', value: 'Club, regional and national-level taekwondo' },
          ].map(c => (
            <div class="bg-white rounded-lg p-5 shadow-sm border border-gray-100">
              <p class="font-body text-xs text-gray-400 uppercase tracking-wider mb-1">{c.label}</p>
              <p class="font-display font-bold text-xl text-navy">{c.value}</p>
            </div>
          ))}
        </div>

        <p class="font-body text-gray-600 text-lg leading-relaxed mb-4">
          Michael has dedicated nine years to coaching taekwondo and supports athletes as a coach, competitor and tournament organiser. He holds a 2nd Dan black belt and World Taekwondo and Kenya Taekwondo Federation certificates.
        </p>
        <p class="font-body text-gray-600 text-lg leading-relaxed">
          As the founder of Charles Michael Sports Hub, Michael is building a home for Kenyan athletes that takes talent seriously from the first class and supports young people as they progress.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Founding team -->
  <section class="py-20 bg-white">
    <div class="max-w-7xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8">
      <div class="text-center mb-12 reveal">
        <p class="section-subtitle">The Founding Team</p>
        <h2 class="section-title">Building the Hub Together</h2>
        <p class="font-body text-gray-600 text-lg max-w-2xl mx-auto mt-4">
          Meet the people helping shape the Hub through taekwondo, community programmes and organisational leadership.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="grid lg:grid-cols-2 gap-8 max-w-6xl mx-auto">
        <article class="card p-6 reveal">
          <div class="grid grid-cols-2 gap-3 mb-5">
            <img
              src="/images/moses-kamau-dojo.webp"
              alt="Moses Kamau in his taekwondo uniform at the Hub"
              class="w-full aspect-[3/4] object-cover object-top rounded-lg"
              loading="lazy"
              decoding="async"
            />
            <img
              src="/images/moses-kamau-portrait.webp"
              alt="Moses Kamau in his black-belt uniform"
              class="w-full aspect-[3/4] object-cover object-top rounded-lg"
              loading="lazy"
              decoding="async"
            />
          </div>
          <p class="section-subtitle">Co-founder - Black Belt</p>
          <h3 class="font-display font-bold text-3xl text-navy mb-3">Moses Kamau</h3>
          <p class="font-body text-gray-600 leading-relaxed">
            Moses is a founding member of Charles Michael Sports Hub and a taekwondo black belt, helping build the Hub’s martial-arts community and athlete pathway.
          </p>
        </article>

        <article class="card p-6 reveal">
          <img
            src="/images/ngugi-kinyanjui.webp"
            alt="Ngugi Kinyanjui, General Manager and founding member"
            class="w-full aspect-[4/3] object-cover object-top rounded-lg mb-5"
            loading="lazy"
            decoding="async"
          />
          <p class="section-subtitle">Co-founder - General Manager</p>
          <h3 class="font-display font-bold text-3xl text-navy mb-3">Ngugi Kinyanjui</h3>
          <p class="font-body text-gray-600 leading-relaxed">
            As a co-founder and General Manager, Ngugi helps guide the Hub’s executive and day-to-day leadership. His work has focused on empowering young people, creating employment opportunities, and developing and delivering programmes that strengthen communities. He also brings experience in running organisations and securing resources to help community initiatives grow.
          </p>
        </article>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Values -->
  <section class="py-20 bg-white">
    <div class="max-w-7xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8">
      <div class="text-center mb-14 reveal">
        <p class="section-subtitle">What We Stand For</p>
        <h2 class="section-title">Our Values</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="grid sm:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-5 gap-6">
        {[
          { icon: '🎯', title: 'Excellence', text: 'We set high standards. For our athletes and for ourselves.' },
          { icon: '🙇', title: 'Respect', text: 'In taekwondo, respect is not optional. It is foundational.' },
          { icon: '🌍', title: 'Inclusion', text: 'Sport should be open to all. We hold places for girls and for families facing financial barriers.' },
          { icon: '🛡️', title: 'Safety', text: 'Every athlete, especially children, trains in a safe, vetted environment.' },
          { icon: '⚖️', title: 'Integrity', text: "We say what we mean, publish what we know, and mark what we don't." },
        ].map((v, i) => (
          <div class="card p-6 text-center reveal" style={`transition-delay: ${i * 80}ms`}>
            <div class="text-4xl mb-3">{v.icon}</div>
            <h3 class="font-display font-bold text-2xl text-navy mb-2">{v.title}</h3>
            <p class="font-body text-gray-600 text-sm leading-relaxed">{v.text}</p>
          </div>
        ))}
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Roadmap -->
  <section class="py-20 bg-navy text-white">
    <div class="max-w-5xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8">
      <div class="text-center mb-14 reveal">
        <p class="section-subtitle text-red-brand">Where We're Going</p>
        <h2 class="font-display font-black text-6xl text-white">The Roadmap</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="space-y-0">
        {[
          {
            stage: '01', title: 'Foundation', status: 'Now',
            text: 'Establish the academy in Limuru. Recruit and train junior and senior athletes. Build a coaching team. Run the first internal and open club competitions.',
            current: true,
          },
          {
            stage: '02', title: 'Prove', status: 'Near term',
            text: 'Host the Mount Kenya International Taekwondo Open Tournament, demonstrate event management capability, and build relationships with KTF, coaches and clubs across Kenya.',
            current: false,
          },
          {
            stage: '03', title: 'Build and Host', status: 'Long term',
            text: 'Apply (through KTF as the appropriate body) for World Taekwondo recognition of the Charles Michael International Open. Host an event on the global calendar.',
            current: false,
          },
        ].map((step, i) => (
          <div class={`flex gap-6 items-start pb-10 reveal ${i < 2 ? 'border-l-2 border-red-brand/30 ml-6 pl-8' : 'ml-6 pl-8'}`} style={`transition-delay: ${i * 100}ms`}>
            <div class={`flex-shrink-0 -ml-14 w-12 h-12 rounded-full flex items-center justify-center font-display font-black text-xl ${step.current ? 'bg-red-brand text-white' : 'bg-navy-light border-2 border-blue-400 text-blue-200'}`}>
              {step.stage}
            </div>
            <div>
              <p class={`font-body text-xs uppercase tracking-widest mb-1 ${step.current ? 'text-red-brand' : 'text-blue-300'}`}>{step.status}</p>
              <h3 class="font-display font-bold text-4xl text-white mb-3">{step.title}</h3>
              <p class="font-body text-blue-100 text-lg leading-relaxed">{step.text}</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        ))}
      </div>
      <div class="mt-8 text-center reveal">
        <a href="/pathway" class="btn-secondary text-xl px-8 py-4">Understand the Full Pathway →</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

</BaseLayout>
